    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated September 2026</p>

    <p class="intro">BridleNav is a GPS navigation app designed specifically for horse riders. By
      downloading and using BridleNav you agree to these Terms of Service. Please read them
      carefully.</p>

    <h2>1. About BridleNav</h2>
    <p>The app is provided by BridleNav Limited, a company registered in England and Wales (company
      number 17461028) whose registered office is Acorn Business Park, 7 Commercial Gate, Mansfield,
      NG18 1EX. In these terms, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; and &ldquo;our&rdquo; mean
      BridleNav Limited.</p>

    <h2>2. Navigation disclaimer</h2>
    <p>BridleNav is a navigation aid only. Routes, directions and mapping data are provided for
      guidance purposes and may not always be accurate, up to date or suitable for your horse and
      riding ability.</p>
    <p>It is your responsibility as a rider to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Assess whether a route is suitable for you and your horse</li>
      <li>Obey all road traffic laws and bridleway regulations</li>
      <li>Wear appropriate safety equipment at all times</li>
      <li>Make your own judgement in all riding situations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We accept no liability for any accidents, injuries, losses or damages arising from use of the
      app or its routes.</p>

    <h2>3. Emergency SOS</h2>
    <p>BridleNav includes an emergency SOS feature that sends your location and a map link to a
      pre-saved emergency contact and provides the option to call 999.</p>
    <p>This feature is a supplementary safety tool only. It requires a working mobile data or
      internet connection to send location messages. BridleNav cannot guarantee delivery of emergency
      messages and is not a substitute for calling 999 directly.</p>
    <p>Always tell someone where you are riding and when you expect to return. Do not rely solely on
      BridleNav SOS in an emergency.</p>

    <h2>4. Your account</h2>
    <p>You can browse routes without an account, but you need one to subscribe. Accounts are created
      with your email address, and you sign in using a six-digit code sent to that address. BridleNav
      is for riders aged 13 and over, and we ask you to confirm this when you create an account.</p>
    <p>You are responsible for keeping access to your email account secure, and for any activity
      carried out through your BridleNav account.</p>
    <p>You can delete your account at any time from within the app, in Settings. Deleting your
      account removes your account record and profile from our systems.</p>

    <h2>5. Subscription and payments</h2>
    <p>BridleNav is available on a subscription basis. Subscriptions are managed through the Google
      Play Store and Apple App Store.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the renewal date</li>
      <li>You can manage or cancel your subscription in your device&rsquo;s app store settings</li>
      <li>Refunds are subject to the relevant app store&rsquo;s refund policy</li>
      <li>Prices may change with reasonable notice</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>All content within BridleNav &mdash; including route data, parking information, descriptions,
